# Jadzi, Steward of Fate enters prepared (CR 722.3a) and "draw two cards, then discard two cards": Bot1 draws Mox Pearl and Mox
# Emerald (not a third card) and discards both Plains. Turn 3 Bot1 casts the Oracle's Gift copy from exile for X=1 ({1}{1}{U}):
# one 0/0 green and blue Fractal token with one counter; Jadzi is unprepared, then bounced by Unsummon and recast on turn 5
# (prepared again). Bot2 made its own Fractal the same way on turn 4. The turn 5 copy for X=2 (Black Lotus' UUU and two Moxen)
# makes two Fractals and the sentence ends at "then" (CR 608.2c): all three of Bot1's Fractals get two counters, the older
# 1/1 becoming 3/3 and the new two 2/2, while Bot2's Fractal stays 1/1 ("each Fractal you control").

